  "foaf:name": "Growing Oceans for Tongan Climate Resilience",
  "sdo:name": "Growing Oceans for Tongan Climate Resilience",
  "sdo:description": "Growing Oceans and the Kingdom of Tonga are collaborating on the science we need to leverage biological nitrogen fixation to support ocean health and climate stability in the South Pacific. By accelerating the evaluation of emerging phytoplankton “blue carbon” solutions, we can see if it is a fit for adoption as a science-based solution on the 2030 Agenda timeline. If so, the results will advance a holistic, nature-based approach to restoring open-ocean ecosystems, protecting biodiversity, and sequestering carbon at a scale relevant to global climate mitigation. For our partners and stakeholders in Tonga, this will be a timely opportunity to incorporate open-ocean nature-based solutions into their new Ocean Management Bill framework and their revised National Plan. This potential to realize Blue Economy revenue streams for this climate vulnerable nation would in turn relieve economic pressures favoring overfishing and consideration of seabed mining programs.",
